    "sentence_translations": [
      "Idioms about Chickens",
      "",
      "It’s the year of the Rooster in China.",
      "You can see various Chicken-decorations in restaurants and shopping malls.",
      "Chinese people believe the chicken to be a lucky animal.",
      "However, the interesting thing is, most of the idioms about chickens and dogs are derogatory.",
      "",
      "For example, “Chicken flies, dog jumps”.",
      "It means the chicken flies away scared, and the dog jumps with fright.",
      "It describes a turmoil caused by panic.",
      "“A mouse came into the house last night and caused a turmoil. Everyone slept badly.”",
      "",
      "Another example is “stealing chicken, touching dog”, meaning to steal thing that are not very expensive.",
      "“He doesn’t have a job, and likes stealing things in the shopping mall. He was caught by police last week.”"
    ]
  }
